{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Arial;}}\f0\fs22 {\b\fs32 Lumina LW-9 Top-Load Washing Machine - User Manual}\par\par Model LW-9. Read this manual before using your washing machine.\par\par {\b\fs26 Safety}\par Unplug the washing machine before cleaning or maintenance.\par Never open the lid while the drum is spinning. The lid lock releases 2 minutes after the cycle ends.\par Do not wash items stained with petrol, oil or solvents.\par \par {\b\fs26 Installation}\par Place the LW-9 on a level floor and adjust the four feet until it does not rock.\par Connect the inlet hose to a cold-water tap. Water pressure must be between 0.1 MPa and 0.8 MPa.\par The drain hose must be between 80 cm and 110 cm above the floor.\par \par {\b\fs26 Programs}\par Normal: everyday cotton, 9 kg maximum load, about 58 minutes.\par Delicate: silk and wool, 2 kg maximum load, about 40 minutes.\par Speed Wash: lightly soiled clothes, 3 kg maximum load, 22 minutes.\par Tub Clean: run once every 30 washes with the drum empty to keep the tub fresh.\par \par {\b\fs26 Child Lock}\par To turn on the child lock, press and hold the Start/Pause and Spin buttons together for 4 seconds. A key symbol appears on the display. Repeat to turn it off.\par \par {\b\fs26 Detergent}\par Use high-efficiency (HE) detergent only. Use about 35 ml for a full load of normally soiled laundry.\par Pour liquid fabric softener into the blue dispenser, never directly onto clothes.\par \par {\b\fs26 Cleaning the Lint Filter}\par Clean the lint filter once a month. Lift the filter out of the top of the agitator, rinse it under running water and push it back until it clicks.\par \par {\b\fs26 Error Codes}\par \trowd\cellx1500\cellx4500\cellx9000 \intbl Code\cell \intbl Meaning\cell \intbl What to do\cell \row \trowd\cellx1500\cellx4500\cellx9000 \intbl F01\cell \intbl No water is entering\cell \intbl Check that the tap is open and the inlet hose is not kinked.\cell \row \trowd\cellx1500\cellx4500\cellx9000 \intbl F07\cell \intbl The drain pump is blocked\cell \intbl Clean the pump filter behind the lower front panel.\cell \row \trowd\cellx1500\cellx4500\cellx9000 \intbl F12\cell \intbl The lid lock has failed\cell \intbl Close the lid firmly. If F12 returns, call service.\cell \row \trowd\cellx1500\cellx4500\cellx9000 \intbl UB\cell \intbl Unbalanced load\cell \intbl Spread the laundry evenly and restart the cycle.\cell \row \pard\par {\b\fs26 Warranty}\par The LW-9 has a 3-year warranty on parts and labour and a 12-year warranty on the motor.\par \par {\b\fs26 Customer Support}\par Lumina customer support: 1-800-555-0110, Monday to Friday, 8 am to 6 pm. Email: help@lumina.example.com.\par \par }